Z||000000||ragilmore||08-31-2001||11:19 AM|||| Is it easy to tell the diffrence in motor's in the car 2.8,3.1,3.2,3.4? any help? thank's Richard||||reg||1
Z||000001||85SE||08-31-2001||11:35 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ragilmore:<BR><B> Is it easy to tell the diffrence in motor's in the car 2.8,3.1,3.2,3.4? any help? thank's Richard</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Richard:<P>Welcome to the forum!  Stock, only the 2.8 lt came in the Fiero - it predates all the other engines you've listed.  The 3.1 is a later version of the 2.8 (bored if I recall correctly) and the 3.4 is sort of a later version of the 3.1 (stroked) - it's a common swap as the Fiero intake and other accessories bolt up to it, with the exception of having to relocate the starter to the opposite side of the engine depending on which vehicle the engine originally came out of.  There's tons of info on that here on the forum - try a search for "3.4 swap" or something similar. <P>I don't recall hearing of a 3.2 lt motor in GM's line, unless you can create one from a 3.1 on a small overbore or something.<P>If a 3.4 has been swapped in for the 2.8 and it's been done so that the car still looks stock, I believe it's quite difficult to tell as the engines look so much alike - perhaps one of the 3.4 people can enlighten.  But a 3.1 can be made from a 2.8 block when it's rebuilt.<P>So the short answer to your question:  It's not easy to tell.  Unless one car is so much more powerful than the other  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> - the 3.4 is putting out usually around 180 hp to the 140 of the 2.8 high output (Fiero engine) or 140-155 of the later 3.1 lt engines.<P>Hope this isn't too confusing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> and that it helped somewhat.<P>------------------<BR>Andrew Menchions - 85SE - AKA Fieroless in Newfoundland||||reg||2
